From 02421fb9d044ccb631263751934ed4ce96f2e7ec Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 17:45:17 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] unify: compatibility layer for the four models built with
 older closed objects

GT-BE98 and GT-BE19000 (ASUS GPL 102_39274) and BQ16 and BQ16 Pro (102_39256) move onto this
tree while keeping the closed objects of their own GPL drop. The open source here calls a few
functions that only the newer closed objects carry; this change provides them for those four
models only, behind one build switch.

- RTCONFIG_REAPER_LEGACY_BLOBS (config.in), set through a REAPER_LEGACY_BLOBS=y token in the
  four model blocks, which move into canon's target.mak verbatim from the 3006.102.8 line.
- rc/reaper_legacy_blobs_shim.c and httpd/reaper_legacy_blobs_httpd.c, weak definitions, each
  keeping the behaviour the model's own firmware had: the Wi-Fi generation reported to AiMesh
  nodes, the raw-WDS test of the guest-SDN WDS fix, the LAN-only rule for telnetd_enable, and
  the three helpers the per-tree reaper_chanlist_shim.c used to provide (now retired).
- rc/usb.c: a one-argument find_dms_dbdir_candidate() for closed objects compiled against the
  older form, bounded at the media-server path size.
- httpd: upload_config_sync.cgi is not served on these models (CVE-2026-19386).
- BQ16 and BQ16 Pro keep their firmware's switch-init timing (init_switch_pre() after
  start_services()), without the LAN port power-cycle at that late point, and their stock
  Broadcom licence set (targets/pakl/legacy-39256).

Every other model builds exactly as before: the switch is off by default.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
